.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vite/
config/*.user.json
config/user.json
app/config/user.json
app/config/*.user.json
data/conversation_memory.jsonl
data/crashlog.txt
# Minidumps from the native-crash handler: ~1 MB of process memory each,
# and process memory is the same personal data as the database.
data/crash-*.dmp
# Runtime prompt-cache diagnostics; generated only when cache logging is enabled.
data/prompt-cache.jsonl
# Legacy runtime artifact from the removed SelfImageWorker; still ignored so
# any stale local copy stays untracked. Aiko's self-model is now concept-driven.
# The human-authored persona (aiko_companion.txt) stays tracked.
data/persona/self_image.txt
data/*.db
data/*.db-shm
data/*.db-wal
# Anything derived from the database is the same personal data: chat history,
# memories, the concept graph. ``data/*.db`` only matches names *ending* in
# .db, so a pre-migration copy like chat_sessions.db.pre-l22-<stamp>.bak was
# untracked but not ignored -- one ``git add .`` from being published.
data/*.db.*
data/*.bak
data/*.sqlite
data/*.sqlite3
models/
data/browser-profile/
*.wav
# The guard has to cover every format the studio accepts, or it only
# guards the format we happened to think of. voices/sounds/ arrived as
# mp3 and was untracked but not ignored -- the same near-miss the
# data/*.db comment above records, one ``git add .`` from publishing
# somebody else's audio.
*.mp3
*.flac
*.ogg
*.opus
*.m4a
# One carve-out. The blanket rule above is a licensing guard -- audition
# material comes from all over and none of it should reach a commit by
# accident -- but it also swallowed the only portable copy of Aiko's own
# voice. voices/ holds two pocket-tts speaker states and no audio, so
# without this line her voice is recoverable only by running the engine
# we are evaluating replacements for. Generated by
# tools/tts_lab/voicebank.py from our own model, so nothing here is
# anyone else's to license.
!voices/reference/aiko_reference.wav
!voices/reference/manifest.json
# Reference sets built in the studio (tools/tts_lab/refset.py). Their wavs
# are already covered above, but the manifest beside them is not -- and a
# manifest whose audio is ignored is a list of somebody else's filenames
# and nothing usable. The one committed set is carved out just above.
voices/*/manifest.json
voices/*/parts/
# Audition output is regenerable in a minute and there is a lot of it.
voices/audition/
# Studio scratch: uploaded references and audition renders.
voices/studio/
# Licensed third-party voice assets, present only as cloning references.
# Directory rule as well as the extension rules above, so dropping a
# .zip or a .json of transcripts beside them stays out too. Bought for
# use elsewhere, which does not extend to redistributing them here.
voices/sounds/
# Generated training datasets (tools/tts_lab/dataset.py). Hundreds of
# clips plus manifests, all reproducible from the committed reference
# voice, so the recipe is worth versioning and the output is not.
voices/datasets/
# Per-engine venvs for the TTS lab (tools/tts_lab/envs.py). Disposable by
# design: candidate engines pin dependencies that would wreck the app's
# venv, so each gets its own and deleting it uninstalls the experiment.
.venvs/
*.log
*.log.*
realtimesst.log
data/lancedb/
data/documents/
data/attachments/
data/personas/
data/plugins/
data/plugins-deps/
# L45 gate-tuner state. Derived from this machine's concept graph, so it
# is the same personal data as the database it was measured from, and it
# is rewritten on every tuning run.
data/tuning/
plugins/*/config/user.json
web/src-tauri/target/
web/src-tauri/gen/
.playwright-mcp/**
tmp
